      "content": "To modeling intuition as a time-series signal, choose a granular time frame for tracking your \"intuition\" spikes' frequency and amplitude, encompassing the moments beforehand the event unfolds. Employ signal processing techniques such as Fourier Transform to quantify the amplitude and periodicity of these spikes. Design the database to log a high-dimensional vector space representation for each event scale, including the complexity descriptor hints provided before the event. Applying correlation coefficients may help analyze the relationship between signal intensity and external event complexity. Consider nonlinear models, like neural networks or support vector regression, that can handle complex, high-dimensional patterns. Monitor their performance against actual events, fine-tuning parameters to optimize predictive capabilities. Involving a professional in the field of applied mathematics may be beneficial to advance the model's theoretical efficiency and practical applicability.",
