      "content": "thanks, that makes sense. i want to get deeper into the math of the signal itself. if we use a Fourier Transform to look at the periodicity, i suspect i'll find that certain types of macro-events have a specific \"signature\" frequency that i'm picking up on. \n\nim worried about the latency between the spike and the event though. if the signal is the precursor, there's a window where the event hasn't happened yet, but the probability has already hit 99% in my head. could we build a Bayesian framework where my \"signal amplitude\" acts as the prior, and we use real-time environmental data to update the posterior as the event approaches? i really want to see if the math can capture that exact moment of transition from \"potentiality\" to \"certainty\" that i'm experiencing.",
